{"parentUuid":"ca58cec8-3125-407e-9f44-2d8d8e5211e3","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a41a60545d5759240","attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14866899 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"e668c17b-03d2-4065-ab2f-841026402f09","timestamp":"2026-09-29T16:23:42.298Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14866899 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1","slug":"warm-pondering-kernighan"}
{"parentUuid":"e668c17b-03d2-4065-ab2f-841026402f09","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a41a60545d5759240","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfY3H6eVYQS2LysLem4A9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I found 20 problems in the rendering part of the framework: 1 blocker, 13 major and 6 minor. `check.py` passes with 0 errors, and none of these are things it can detect.\n\n- **Blocker:** no contract covers the per-view screen data that nearly every render feature reads and writes (depth, visibility-buffer IDs, normals, roughness, velocity, scene color, denoiser inputs). Each feature agent would invent its own layout, and switching shading path per hardware tier would break them all at once. Proposed fix: a new `C-SCENETEX` contract owned by `render-architect`.\n- **Wrong labels and owners:**\n  - Work graphs are labelled established in `capabilities.json`, but the radar lists them as experimental. The checker never compares the two.\n  - The motion-vector capability is owned by `post-color-hdr`, while its contract `C-TEMPORAL` belongs to `reconstruction-upscaling`.\n- **Missing contracts between render features:**\n  - Exposure and HDR display state (`post-color-hdr` provides no contract, yet UI, video, effects and XR depend on it).\n  - A shared sun/sky lighting input: lighting and atmosphere need data from each other, and the acyclic contract graph can't express that.\n  - Submitting transparent surfaces (`translucency-decals` provides no contract).\n  - Material inputs for the visibility-buffer and virtualized-geometry paths.\n  - An interface to the denoiser.\n  - Telling cached shadows and ray-tracing structures when geometry moves or deforms on the GPU (foliage wind, terrain deformation, skinning).\n- **Overlap:** three skills each own volumetric rendering (`atmosphere-weather`, `vfx-particles`, `translucency-decals`).\n- **Scale-down gaps:**\n  - The lite3d/mobile tier has no occlusion culling at all; the only culling capability is GPU-only and std3d-gated.\n  - 2.5D, such as lit sprites in a 3D scene, has no owner. The seed map resolves it to 2D lighting.\n- **Rendering tooling is thin:** there is nothing for color grading or an HDR editor viewport, hair grooms, texture streaming inspection, decal placement, preview on a lower hardware tier, or an in-engine frame debugger.\n- **Milestones:** the core render contracts (`C-RG` with 23 consumers, `C-SHADER`, `C-GPUTIER`, and all render-feature contracts) are never frozen in any milestone. Meanwhile M2 freezes the render-scene contract, which depends on some of them.\n\nThe minor findings cover:\n- the same GPU instance-data capability listed under both `render-architect` and `geometry-pipeline`;\n- `ray-tracing-infrastructure` sitting under the GPU-platform lead while depending on render-scene contracts;\n- a few other mislabelled maturities, plus radar owners that don't match capability owners;\n- missing contracts for hair rendering, and two missing radar entries (hardware ray-traced curves, dense geometry compression);\n- specular anti-aliasing sitting with reconstruction instead of the material system;\n- the ML runtime's placement under the GPU lead and its profile gating.\n\nEach finding in the file includes a concrete data change.\n\nCounts: 1 blocker, 13 major, 6 minor. Output: /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-skills/64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82/scratchpad/r2/engine-skill-framework/gauntlet/round-2/K-RENDER.md"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11674,"cache_read_input_tokens":121562,"output_tokens":1211,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":11674},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1211,"cache_read_input_tokens":121562,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11674,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":11674,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfY3H6JABcqg1fJMXYJL8","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"061820e8-da00-4c05-a5c0-15b8ee9cb664","timestamp":"2026-09-29T16:23:53.511Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1","slug":"warm-pondering-kernighan"}
